WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.855 --> 00:00:17.236
September 10 Dear Daddy Longlegs, School opens in about two weeks.

2
00:00:18.336 --> 00:00:22.458
I'll be glad to start working again, although I've worked quite a bit this summer.

3
00:00:23.698 --> 00:00:26.299
I wrote six short stories and seven poems.

4
00:00:27.739 --> 00:00:30.900
I sent some to magazines, but they were all quickly rejected.

5
00:00:35.064 --> 00:00:37.366
Jervie read a few of my stories when he was here.

6
00:00:38.587 --> 00:00:42.809
He brought the mail in every day, so I couldn't hide the rejection letters from him.

7
00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:46.132
"What's this, another rejection?"

8
00:00:47.553 --> 00:00:49.434
Jervie tossed a thick envelope at me.

9
00:00:50.495 --> 00:00:51.956
I glanced at the return address.

10
00:00:53.397 --> 00:00:54.978
It was from a magazine in New York.

11
00:00:54.998 --> 00:00:57.340
"Yep," I replied.

12
00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.901
"Open it," Jervie said.

13
00:01:01.182 --> 00:01:03.324
I opened the envelope and read the brief note.

14
00:01:04.288 --> 00:01:06.830
"My story isn't quite right for them," I said.

15
00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:09.211
"But I don't mind.

16
00:01:10.132 --> 00:01:11.973
Writing the story was good practice."

17
00:01:13.514 --> 00:01:14.455
"Let me see your story."

18
00:01:15.616 --> 00:01:17.697
Jervie took it and sat down in the parlor.

19
00:01:19.058 --> 00:01:20.799
I paced in front of him while he read.

20
00:01:20.819 --> 00:01:24.542
"I don't care that it was rejected," I mumbled.

21
00:01:24.562 --> 00:01:26.983
"But I really hope you like it."

22
00:01:27.003 --> 00:01:31.547
"Judy, this story is dreadful!"

23
00:01:32.447 --> 00:01:33.448
Jervie looked up at me.

24
00:01:34.592 --> 00:01:36.854
"It's even worse than the last one you sent out.

25
00:01:37.654 --> 00:01:40.116
You have absolutely no idea what you're talking about!

26
00:01:40.896 --> 00:01:42.758
People don't act like this in the city!"

27
00:01:44.399 --> 00:01:44.939
I laughed.

28
00:01:44.959 --> 00:01:49.342
"Don't worry about hurting my feelings!

29
00:01:50.163 --> 00:01:51.804
Just blurt out the awful truth."

30
00:01:52.304 --> 00:01:53.845
I said, making a face at him.

31
00:01:54.786 --> 00:01:55.726
What else could I do?

32
00:01:57.447 --> 00:01:58.928
Jervie tried to hide a smile.

33
00:01:58.948 --> 00:02:00.810
"What are you working on now?"

34
00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:03.852
"A story set at college.

35
00:02:05.048 --> 00:02:08.531
But I don't want to show it to you, if you're just going to make fun of it."

36
00:02:09.692 --> 00:02:11.434
I snatched my story from his hand.

37
00:02:11.454 --> 00:02:15.598
"At least you know something about college," he muttered.

38
00:02:15.618 --> 00:02:18.981
"It might be more convincing than the one you sent to the magazine."

39
00:02:19.001 --> 00:02:22.824
"Well, maybe I'll let you see it when I'm finished."

40
00:02:25.166 --> 00:02:28.369
So a couple days later, I showed him my new story.

41
00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:31.352
Amazingly, he liked it!

42
00:02:34.336 --> 00:02:37.857
He had a secretary type it for me, and I sent it to a magazine.

43
00:02:40.778 --> 00:02:42.598
But I haven't heard anything yet.

44
00:02:43.559 --> 00:02:45.379
At least it wasn't rejected right away!

45
00:02:46.859 --> 00:02:48.680
Jervie has gone back to New York City.

46
00:02:50.841 --> 00:02:53.121
Everybody misses him, especially me.

47
00:02:54.461 --> 00:02:55.342
I'm finding Mrs.

48
00:02:55.402 --> 00:02:57.422
Semple's conversation pretty boring.

49
00:02:59.023 --> 00:03:08.921
Yours ever, Judy September 14 Dear Daddy Longlegs, The postman just arrived with two letters for me.

50
00:03:10.922 --> 00:03:14.463
The magazine accepted my story and will pay me fifty dollars.

51
00:03:15.803 --> 00:03:16.503
I'm an AUTHOR!

52
00:03:18.324 --> 00:03:19.964
The second letter is from the college.

53
00:03:21.105 --> 00:03:25.406
I've won a scholarship that will pay for my tuition and board for two years.

54
00:03:27.566 --> 00:03:32.868
The scholarship is for someone who has done exceptionally well in English and has also succeeded in other

55
00:03:32.928 --> 00:03:36.853
subjects. I applied at the end of the school year.

56
00:03:37.733 --> 00:03:42.076
But I was afraid I wouldn't get it because I'd failed those two exams my freshman year.

57
00:03:43.116 --> 00:03:44.937
Now I won't be such a burden to you.

58
00:03:46.578 --> 00:03:48.259
All I'll need is my monthly allowance.

59
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.621
I can probably make that amount writing or tutoring.

60
00:03:52.942 --> 00:03:54.923
So I'll eventually be able to pay you back.

61
00:03:56.004 --> 00:03:57.845
I can't wait for school to start!

62
00:03:59.225 --> 00:04:09.542
Yours ever, Jerusha Abbott, author of "When the Sophomores Won the Game" September 26 Dear Daddy Longlegs, I'm

63
00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:12.064
back at college, where I am now a junior!

64
00:04:13.885 --> 00:04:15.846
I'm rooming with Sallie and Julia again.

65
00:04:17.187 --> 00:04:19.028
Our room is very nice this year.

66
00:04:21.109 --> 00:04:26.792
Julia, who has an unlimited allowance, spent a lot of money on furniture and rugs.

67
00:04:29.593 --> 00:04:34.336
I have been busy hemming curtains for our study, and welcoming back fifty dear friends.

68
00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.822
I'm also unpacking two trunks full of clothes.

69
00:04:40.143 --> 00:04:42.705
Quite a change from when I arrived here two years ago!

70
00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:47.589
I received your letter—I mean, your secretary's letter.

71
00:04:49.251 --> 00:04:51.072
I know you don't want me to pay you back.

72
00:04:52.313 --> 00:04:53.494
But I want to do that.

73
00:04:55.516 --> 00:04:58.758
And with this scholarship, I'll owe you less money than I once thought.

74
00:04:59.459 --> 00:05:02.001
I don't understand your objections to the scholarship.

75
00:05:02.821 --> 00:05:05.884
But it doesn't matter because I've already accepted the scholarship.

76
00:05:07.036 --> 00:05:17.845
Affectionately, Judy September 30 Dear Daddy Longlegs, I can't believe you're still complaining about that scholarship.

77
00:05:18.966 --> 00:05:20.808
I never knew such a stubborn man.

78
00:05:21.669 --> 00:05:24.291
You say that I shouldn't accept gifts from strangers.

79
00:05:25.532 --> 00:05:27.353
Well, what do you think you are?

80
00:05:28.474 --> 00:05:30.696
I wouldn't know you if I met you on the street!

81
00:05:31.897 --> 00:05:33.799
Besides, this scholarship isn't a gift.

82
00:05:35.232 --> 00:05:37.034
It's more like a prize that I've earned.

83
00:05:38.315 --> 00:05:40.136
I refuse to give up the scholarship.

84
00:05:41.657 --> 00:05:45.160
And if you keep bothering me about it, I won't accept your allowance.

85
00:05:46.622 --> 00:05:48.723
I'll spend endless hours tutoring freshmen.

86
00:05:49.884 --> 00:05:54.168
You say that if I take the scholarship, I'm depriving another girl of an education.

87
00:05:55.529 --> 00:05:59.893
If you care so much about educating girls, send another orphan to college!

88
00:06:01.894 --> 00:06:03.776
I've given in to your demands in the past.

89
00:06:04.492 --> 00:06:06.738
But this time I will stand FIRM.

90
00:06:08.061 --> 00:06:12.171
Yours, with my mind completely made up, Jerusha Abbott
